WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.660
- Please welcome comedy
legend, beautiful woman,

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.194
and my dear friend, Molly Shannon.

00:00:07.194 --> 00:00:12.194
(audience cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.264 --> 00:00:16.168
By the way, you look so beautiful.

00:00:16.168 --> 00:00:17.168
- So do you.

00:00:18.173 --> 00:00:20.075
Hi, you guys.

00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:21.325
This is so fun.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.380
You look so pretty, Drew.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.528
- Oh, Molly, I--
- Wait do I stand here?

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.230
I'm so nervous.
- I love you so much.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.220
Why don't you come take a seat over here?

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.520
They say it's the better lighting.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.010
So I'd rather you have that.
- Okay, good, good.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.160
- Molly and I, we made really
close friends on the movie

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.610
and we continued that friendship,

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:48.610
and I was always able to talk
to you about life and family

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.720
and friendship and the real stuff

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.170
that's important between girlfriends.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.960
- Yes, Drew, that's so sweet.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.730
And women need other
women, and it's so nice.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:00.250
And you know, I feel
the same way about you.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.160
- We had a great time making that movie.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.710
- And you were a real
role model for me on set.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.470
I really learned how to
behave in show business

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.932
from Drew Barrymore.

00:01:12.932 --> 00:01:15.082
(audience applauding)
Yeah, you taught me.

00:01:16.368 --> 00:01:21.368
- Well, that makes me happy
because you were also my Velcro

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.390
when I would go to Saturday Night Live,

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.280
which was my most important institution.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.520
I first hosted in 1982 at seven years old.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.857
I'm still the youngest host.
- Oh my god.

00:01:34.857 --> 00:01:35.717
That's crazy.

00:01:35.717 --> 00:01:38.670
- I'm like seriously going to be so happy

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.820
and slightly resent any child that takes

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:44.300
that title away from me.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.202
I'll be like, "I'm so happy for you."

00:01:46.202 --> 00:01:49.760
(audience laughing)

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.541
And of course, my favorite
segment on the show was

00:01:54.541 --> 00:01:56.958
(clapping)

00:01:56.958 --> 00:01:58.676
- [Both] Dog show!

00:01:58.676 --> 00:02:00.926
(laughing)

00:02:02.652 --> 00:02:05.950
- And Drew was so funny.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.350
I actually put it on my Instagram

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.630
because it is my favorite dog show.

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:11.070
She played Michael Trulio.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.070
It's one of my favorite performances.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.310
You embraced Michael Trulio.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.120
- Now, I wanna wuickly talk to you

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:23.120
about the show of the year, "White Lotus."

00:02:23.682 --> 00:02:26.682
(audience cheering)

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.860
- I wanted to do a really good job

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.330
'cause I knew it was a really good part.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.430
We shot it in Maui.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.770
We all lived at The Four Seasons.

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:36.640
It was a dream job.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.290
I got to bring my kids cause
they were in remote school,

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:40.867
and they would, I would, I'd be like,

00:02:40.867 --> 00:02:42.180
"I'm going to shoot a scene in the lobby."

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.810
And they would like to snorkel

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.187
and then walk back with
their gear on and be like,

00:02:46.187 --> 00:02:47.560
"Hi, Molly. Hi, Mike."

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.870
And it was the greatest job for a mom.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.720
- Now you have another show on HBO Max,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.510
and you are a talk show
host in this amazing series

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.070
that is going into season two.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.670
It's wildly popular.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.220
It's called "The Other Two."

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.630
It's on HBO Max.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.650
Take a look.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.660
- Do you have a sad, grumpy
friend who needs a pick-me-up?

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.700
Then enter them to win a
shopping spree with me, Pat,

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.540
sponsored by MasterCard, but
paid for by me personally.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.880
- Great. Number 13.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.860
- [Producer] Hold for camera reset.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:17.170
- Hey, Brookie, we're really
scheduling a lot of these,

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.003
but don't forget

00:03:18.003 --> 00:03:20.470
that I have Lisa son's
wedding in Ohio next month.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.410
- Keep reading.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.800
- Do you like weddings?

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.330
Win a chance to come to my
friend, Lisa son's wedding

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.790
in Ohio next month.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.817
Oh. With me, Pat.

00:03:28.817 --> 00:03:29.650
(audience cheering)

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.170
- How do you feel
playing a talk show host?

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.630
- I love playing a talk show host.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:33.463
It's so fun.

00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:37.490
So I'm pretending to do
what you do in real life.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.802
And I have to say, I love it.

00:03:39.802 --> 00:03:42.385
(upbeat music)

